<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="correction"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">PLoS Pathog</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="publisher-id">ppat</journal-id><journal-title>PLoS Pathogens</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">1553-7366</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1553-7374</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Public Library of Science</publisher-name> <publisher-loc>San Francisco, USA</publisher-loc></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">1904409</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.ppat.0030090</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="publisher-id">07-PLPA-CN-0304</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="sici">plpa-03-06-12</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Correction</subject></subj-group><subj-group subj-group-type="Discipline"><subject>Microbiology</subject><subject>Plant Biology</subject></subj-group><subj-group subj-group-type="System Taxonomy"><subject>Arabidopsis</subject><subject>Plant Immune System</subject><subject>type III effector</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Correction: Type III Effector Activation via Nucleotide Binding, Phosphorylation, and Host Target Interaction</article-title><alt-title alt-title-type="running-head">Correction</alt-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Desveaux</surname><given-names>Darrell</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Singer</surname><given-names>Alex U</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>Ai-Jiuan</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>McNulty</surname><given-names>Brian C</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Musslewhite</surname><given-names>Laura</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Nimchuk</surname><given-names>Zachary</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Sondek</surname><given-names>John</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Dangl</surname><given-names>Jeffrey L</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>6</month><year>2007</year></pub-date><pub-date pub-type="epub"><day>29</day><month>6</month><year>2007</year></pub-date><volume>3</volume><issue>6</issue><elocation-id>e90</elocation-id><copyright-statement><bold>Copyright:</bold> &#x000a9; 2007 Sourisseau et al. This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2007</copyright-year><related-article xlink:href="10.1371/journal.ppat.0030048" related-article-type="corrected-article" xlink:title="Research Article" id="RA1" ext-link-type="doi" vol="3" page="e48"><article-title>Type III Effector Activation via Nucleotide Binding, Phosphorylation, and Host Target Interaction</article-title></related-article><counts><page-count count="1"/></counts><custom-meta-wrap><custom-meta><meta-name>citation</meta-name><meta-value>(2007) Correction: Type III effector activation via nucleotide binding, phosphorylation, and host target interaction. PLoS Pathog 3(6): e90. doi:<ext-link ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1371/journal.ppat.0030090">10.1371/journal.ppat.0030090</ext-link></meta-value></custom-meta></custom-meta-wrap></article-meta></front><body><p>In <italic>PLoS Pathogens,</italic> volume 3, issue 3: <ext-link ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1371/journal.ppat.0030048">10.1371/journal.ppat.0030048</ext-link></p><p>On page 0457, in the first paragraph of the Results section, the above paper states:</p><p>&#x0201c;Additionally, AvrB T182 contacts RIN4 Y151, and AvrB V128 contacts RIN4 D155, S161, and G162&#x0201d;.</p><p>This should read:</p><p>&#x0201c;Additionally, AvrB T182 contacts RIN4 F151, and AvrB V128 contacts RIN4 D155, S161, and A162&#x0201d;.</p><p>Further, in Table 2, line 2, G163 should be A162; and in Table 2, line 9, Y151 should be F151. The corrected table is as follows:</p><table-wrap id="ppat-0030090-t001" content-type="1col" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>List of AvrB Mutations</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ppat.0030090.t001"/></table-wrap><p>The authors regret these errors and thank K. Caldwell and R. Michelmore for alerting us to them.</p></body></article>